# Manual page

.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "August 2026" "Holberton School" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
simple_shell \- simple UNIX command-line interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simple_shell
is a simple UNIX command-line interpreter written in C.

The shell displays a prompt, reads commands from standard input, executes the commands, and displays the prompt again.

.SH INVOCATION
The shell is started by running:

.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
.fi

.SH COMMAND EXECUTION
The shell reads a command from standard input and attempts to execute it.

The shell uses the PATH environment variable to locate executable commands.

If the command cannot be found, an error message is displayed and the shell returns to the prompt.

.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
In interactive mode, the shell displays a prompt and waits for the user to enter a command.

.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
$ ls
$ pwd
$ whoami
.fi

.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
The shell can read commands from standard input.

For example:

.PP
.nf
$ echo "ls" | ./hsh
.fi

.SH ENVIRONMENT
The shell inherits environment variables from its parent process.

The PATH environment variable is used to search for executable commands.

.SH END OF FILE
The shell handles the end-of-file condition.

Pressing Ctrl-D terminates an interactive session.

.SH ERRORS
If a command cannot be found or executed, the shell displays an appropriate error message.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
$ ls
$ pwd
$ whoami
.fi

.SH BUGS
This shell is a simple implementation and does not provide all the features of shells such as bash.

.SH AUTHORS
See the AUTHORS file in the project repository for a list of contributors.
